{"title":"2010-2011 Mock USAJMO Problems/Solutions/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> be positive real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a07fb197df7bb042844b9d1eac083956ce2cf577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />. Prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f38d8c69777a0bdce430ec7ae8fd6be1f6c7561.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3x+1}{y+z}+\\frac{3y+1}{z+x}+\\frac{3z+1}{x+y}\\ge\\frac{4}{2x+y+z}+\\frac{4}{x+2y+z}+\\frac{4}{x+y+2z},\\]\" width=\"505\" height=\"41\" />\nwith equality if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/1/3a1bb32241472c525e5624db47ff8edf81dd33a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010-2011_Mock_USAJMO_Problems/Solutions/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we change the terms using the relationship <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/c/0fce09322356796e6adce205b1e7d6d0b7d7e5ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6e178aa9a273aa35aceaa065ff1efea1fe4054d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{3x+1}{y+z} - \\sum_{cyc}\\frac{4}{2x+y+z}\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/f/91f911e65f445420bfb3cb646130cc110247f54b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\sum_{cyc}(\\frac{4}{y+z}-1) - \\sum_{cyc}\\frac{4}{1+x}= 4\\sum_{cyc} (\\frac{1}{1-x} - \\frac{1}{1+x}) - 9\\]\" width=\"451\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef47264844bf5fb47dff8397893821b6c23d5e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 8\\sum_{cyc} \\frac{x}{1-x^2} - 9\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Then, by Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality, one has:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56ccd7de22803d006c442c0e7169c20eee823070.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc}\\frac{x}{1-x^2} \\cdot \\sum_{cyc} (x-x^3) \\ge (x+y+z)^2 = 1\\]\" width=\"336\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>And by AM-GM, one has:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6afbf88739d5a6595bbad3d659ed25c0951cff9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc} (x-x^3) = 1- \\sum_{cyc} x^3  \\le 1- 3(\\frac{x+y+z}{3})^3 = \\frac{8}{9}\\]\" width=\"391\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f850446f4ca1b6171c4a9dcbd9d2cc46ac94fe5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8\\sum_{cyc} \\frac{x}{1-x^2} - 9 \\ge 8 \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sum_{cyc} (x-x^3)} - 9 \\ge 8 \\cdot \\frac{9}{8} - 9 = 0,\\]\" width=\"438\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>where both equations are true if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598f63638746c8c3c12c7ee6192cc721528f3e10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=z=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"113\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>edited by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Lightest\" title=\"User:Lightest\">User:lightest</a> 17:35, 24 April 2012 (EDT)\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017221519\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.068 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 49/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2510/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11046:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017221519 and revision id 46565. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}